[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515070370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2515070370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2515070370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6O2i","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T16:42:57Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T16:43:53Z","body":"My initial feeling is that using a `Callable()` to call a virtual method doesn't seem like the right way to do it. It's similar to how we still sometimes find code in Godot that does `object->get_script_instance()->call(...)` rather than `GDVIRTUAL_CALL()`, and need to make a bug fix to switch to `GDVIRTUAL_CALL()`.\n\nAlso, looking at some of the examples in the OP, not all of them appear to deal with virtual methods. For example, the `_bake()` methods on `lightmap_gi_editor_plugin.cpp` and `occluder_instance_3d_editor_plugin.cpp` aren't virtual functions, those look like a case where `callable_mp()` should be used just to call a concrete C++ method.\n\nI think only `_render_callback()` on `CompositorEffect` is a virtual method. And in that case, it seems like a bug. I think we should add a `CompositorEffect::_call_render_callback()` method which uses `GDVIRTUAL_CALL()`, and then use `callable_mp(this, &CompositorEffect::_call_render_callback)` to make the `Callable`.\n\nAre there any other examples of this that you are aware of?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515070370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515169478","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2515169478","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2515169478,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6nDG","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T17:26:47Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T17:26:47Z","body":"> Are there any other examples of this that you are aware of?\n\nNo, in fact `CompositorEffect::_render_callback()` is exactly the method that a godot-rust user reported.\n\nAnd as you see from my false-positive-riddled regex, there might be better approaches to finding others 😉 not sure how to do that systematically. Check for every method declared as virtual in `extension_api.json`, whether there's at least one `GDVIRTUAL_CALL` statement in the codebase?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515169478/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515363612","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2515363612","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2515363612,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7Wcc","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T19:04:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T19:04:55Z","body":"I threw together draft PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99981 that does what I described earlier to address `CompositorEffect` specifically\n\n> Check for every method declared as virtual in `extension_api.json`, whether there's at least one `GDVIRTUAL_CALL` statement in the codebase?\n\nThat sounds like it'd be a decent way to check! Of course, it only means that the right thing is being done at least once, not that there is no code doing the wrong thing, but it would have detected this case.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515363612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515606140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2515606140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2515606140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V8Rp8","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T21:40:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T21:40:26Z","body":"That was super fast, thanks a lot! :heart:\n\n---\n\n> That sounds like it'd be a decent way to check!\n\nSo I extracted all virtual functions inside classes declared in `extension_api.json` (just quick&dirty inside godot-rust parsing code).\nLet's call this file `api-declared-virtuals.txt`. Each line is a method name, the file is sorted and unique.\n\nThen, I extracted all `GDVIRTUAL_CALL` statements in the Godot codebase, with their method name, as follows:\n```bash\ncd path/to/godot\n\n# Find all virtual calls in Godot code base\nrg --no-filename --only-matching \"GDVIRTUAL_CALL\\([a-zA-Z0-9_]+\" | sed 's/GDVIRTUAL_CALL(//' \\\n   | sort | uniq > found-virtuals.txt\n```\nNow I have two sorted unique files, I can get the difference.\n```bash\ncomm -23 api-declared-virtuals.txt found-virtuals.txt > never_called.txt\ncomm -13 api-declared-virtuals.txt found-virtuals.txt > called_but_not_exposed.txt\n```\n\nThere's a huge list for `never_called`, which surprises me.\n```bash\n$ wc -l *.txt\n\n 1030 api-declared-virtuals.txt\n    4 called_but_not_exposed.txt\n  507 found-virtuals.txt\n  527 never_called.txt\n```\nI checked a few and many have `GDVIRTUAL_BIND` but no call, which only registers them, no? Can't be that half the virtual methods is never called, what am I missing?\n\nHere are the files, ran on commit 47bc374edf6d2e775a5e6b937dc3fd73cdc6f59b.\n- [api-declared-virtuals.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17999431/api-declared-virtuals.txt)\n- [found-virtuals.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17999430/found-virtuals.txt)\n- [never_called.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17999429/never_called.txt)\n- [called_but_not_exposed.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17999428/called_but_not_exposed.txt)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515606140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524360647","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2524360647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2524360647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Wdq_H","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T22:35:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T22:49:44Z","body":"@Bromeon: Thanks for doing this investigation!\n\n> I checked a few and many have `GDVIRTUAL_BIND` but no call, which only registers them, no? Can't be that half the virtual methods is never called, what am I missing?\n\nAh, I think you're missing the `EXBIND*()` macros. Those can be used to generate the functions that do `GDVIRTUAL_CALL()`. For example, take a look at `PhysicsServer2DExtension` - it uses the `EXBIND*()` macros quite extensively.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524360647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524574552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2524574552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2524574552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WefNY","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T23:03:31Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T23:03:31Z","body":"I just posted PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100126 to address the ones in your [called_but_not_exposed.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17999428/called_but_not_exposed.txt).\n\nTwo of them appear to be false positives (`m_name` and `_create_editor`), but I added the missing `GDVIRTUAL_BIND()` for the other two.\n\n(FYI, the `GDVIRTUAL_BIND()` registers them so they get listed in `extension_api.json` and the documentation, but that isn't necessary for them to work with GDScript, which is probably why no one noticed these were missing.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524574552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525260260","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2525260260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2525260260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhGnk","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T17:52:09Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T17:54:15Z","body":"Cool, thank you!\n\nI tried to look for `EXBIND*` with the following, then prefixed with `_`:\n```bash\nrg --no-filename --only-matching \"EXBIND[A-Za-z0-9_]+\\([a-zA-Z0-9_]+, [a-zA-Z0-9_]+\" | sd \".+, \" \"\" > found-exbinds.txt\nrg --no-filename --only-matching \"EXBIND[A-Za-z0-9_]+\\([a-zA-Z0-9_]+\" | sd \".+, \" \"\" > found-exbinds-2.txt\n```\nWith that (+previous list), I could limit the `never_called_v2.txt` list to 11 entries:\n```\n_body_get_direct_state\n_create_data_channel\n_get_base_script\n_get_contact_collider_object\n_get_language\n_get_space_state\n_make_template\n_put_partial_data\n_render_callback\n_space_get_contacts\n_space_get_direct_state\n```\n\nSome of them seem to be false positives, e.g. my regex didn't catch the star here:\n```cpp\nEXBIND0R(PhysicsDirectSpaceState3D *, get_space_state)\n```\nCould you maybe verify if those virtual methods are truly called or not?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525260260/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2538406219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2538406219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2538406219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XTQFL","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T09:53:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T09:53:37Z","body":"Could anyone verify if the remaining methods [in my comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2525260260) are registered correctly?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2538406219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539110712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2539110712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2539110712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XV8E4","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T14:28:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T14:28:27Z","body":"> Could anyone verify if the remaining methods [in my comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2525260260) are registered correctly?\n\nThanks for the reminder!\n\nI just went through all the items on your list, and most were false positives from `EXBIND*()` with return values with pointers or `Ref<T>` or similar. But there is one true positive!\n\n`StreamPeerExtension::put_partial_data()` is calling the wrong virtual method:\n\n```c++\nError StreamPeerExtension::put_partial_data(const uint8_t *p_data, int p_bytes, int &r_sent) {\n\tError err;\n\tif (GDVIRTUAL_CALL(_put_data, p_data, p_bytes, &r_sent, err)) {\n\t\treturn err;\n\t}\n\tWARN_PRINT_ONCE(\"StreamPeerExtension::_put_partial_data is unimplemented!\");\n\treturn FAILED;\n}\n```\n\nI'll make a PR to fix it in a moment!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539110712/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539128996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99933#issuecomment-2539128996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99933","id":2539128996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XWAik","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsn